<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    What may leave the phone when Android backs the app up (`cloud-backup`, i.e. Google Drive) or
    copies it to a new one (`device-transfer`). Read on API 31+; `backup_rules.xml` says the same
    thing for API 30, which is minSdk.

    An exclude list, not `allowBackup="false"`: the settings are worth restoring. Realm, entity and
    source ids, the endpoint list, per-subject switches, rates, QoS overrides, the operator identity
    and the checklist state all live in `files/datastore/` and are tedious to retype — losing them on
    a phone swap is a real cost with nothing bought for it.

    With no `<include>` anywhere, everything not excluded here is backed up. Adding one would flip
    that: the file becomes an allow-list and anything unlisted stops being backed up, silently.

    Three things must not travel:

    * `tls` — the mTLS material `TlsCredentialStore` imports. `client_key.pem` authenticates this
      phone to the *shared* fleet bus, so a copy in a Google Drive backup, or riding a phone-to-phone
      transfer onto a device nobody enrolled, is exactly the exposure that keeping it out of the APK
      and off external storage was meant to prevent. A restored phone therefore has no credentials
      and says so: `clientConfigJson` throws naming the missing file, which surfaces through
      `statusStore.setupFailed()`. Re-importing is the intended path — enrolment is per device.

    * `recordings` — MCAP files in flight. Cloud backup has a 25 MB quota per app and a file over it
      does not merely get skipped, it fails the whole backup, so a run in progress would quietly cost
      the settings their backup too. A finished recording is copied to Downloads/Logline, which has a
      backup story of its own.

    * `osmdroid` — the map tile cache. Hundreds of MB of re-downloadable data, same quota problem,
      and it is a cache: `TrackMap` rebuilds it from the network.
-->
<data-extraction-rules>
    <cloud-backup>
        <exclude domain="file" path="tls" />
        <exclude domain="file" path="recordings" />
        <exclude domain="file" path="osmdroid" />
    </cloud-backup>
    <device-transfer>
        <exclude domain="file" path="tls" />
        <exclude domain="file" path="recordings" />
        <exclude domain="file" path="osmdroid" />
    </device-transfer>
</data-extraction-rules>
